---
title: Matcha Muffins
image: https://www.chopstickchronicles.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Matcha-Muffin-29.jpg
source: https://www.chopstickchronicles.com/matcha-muffins/#wprm-recipe-container-6150
servings: 6
nutrition:
  calories: 200 kcal
  fat: 9 g
  saturated fat: 5 g
  carbohydrates: 24 g
  sugar: 9 g
  protein: 5 g
  fiber: 1 g
  sodium: 17 mg
  serving size: 1 g
prep time: 15 minutes
cuisine: Japanese
course: Dessert
cook time: 30 minutes
time required: 40 minutes
---

Preheat your oven to 356°F.

Line your #muffin tray{} with cupcake liners.

Sift @all-purpose or cake flour{1%cup}, @matcha powder{2.5%tbsp}, and @baking powder{1%tsp} into a #bowl.

In a separate #bowl, whisk @butter{1/2%stick}(unsalted, room temperature) and @sugar{1/4%cup} until the mixture becomes white.

In a separate #bowl, whisk @egg{1}(room temperature).

Add the egg slowly, in 3-4 parts, to the butter/sugar mixture while mixing, so the egg and butter do not separate.

Fold the sifted flour mixture into the batter with @?toppings{1%tbsp}(kuromame, chocolate chips, chestnut, or any other nut). Avoid over mixing - a little flour is okay.

Mix in @milk{1/4%cup}. 

Pour the batter evenly into prepared liners and top with @?toppings{1%tbsp}(kuromame, chocolate chips, chestnut, or any other nut).

Bake for ~{20%minutes}, setting the oven now to 340°F after inserting the muffins. If under cooked, check every 2 minutes until cooked. Any more than 30 minutes will be too much though.

> While this is a matcha muffin recipe, you can try replacing the matcha with cocoa powder for chocolate muffins.